    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=cTp7e": {
      "title": "Clinical Educator",
      "description": "Clinical Educator - Oral Health - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Clinical Educator - Oral Health Clinical Educator - Oral Health Culturally responsive practice Teach and mentor future oral health therapists in simulation and clinical environments Casual hourly paid appointments during the semester period at North and/or South Campus, Auckland Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. The role sits within the Oral Health discipline in the School of Acute and Primary Health, Faculty of Environmental and Health Sciences at AUT. The school is committed to delivering high-quality, culturally responsive health education and operates a teaching clinic essential for student clinical training, accreditation, and providing accessible oral health services to diverse communities. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi The School of Acute and Primary Health has two casual positions available for a Clinical Educator in the Oral Health department. With the guidance of the Course and Programme Leaders and Head of Department, you will deliver teaching and learning experiences for students enrolled in the oral health programme, including preclinical and clinical practice. The successful applicants will hold a Bachelor’s degree in oral therapy and will have a strong clinical and/or academic background and currently be registered with the Dental Council of New Zealand.  They will embrace the vision and values of the school The positions will work alongside students including Māori and Pacific students so a high level of cultural sensitivity is desired, along with knowledge of kawa and tikanga Māori and mātauranga Māori (Māori knowledge). What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll be part of a values-led university that supports you to thrive in your academic career. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff . About you | Ko wai koe At AUT, academic staff combine teaching, research and engagement to create meaningful impact. You will work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to projects with industry, community and academic partners. We’re looking for academics with curiosity, energy and openness to new ideas , who are committed to collegiality, cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience contributing to Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. The selection criteria sought are: Qualification: A relevant Bachelor’s degree in oral health, oral health therapy, or an equivalent recognised qualification. Current registration with the Dental Council of New Zealand and a current Annual Practising Certificate. Demonstrated recent clinical experience within the relevant oral health scope of practice (restoratives and periodontics). Teaching: Previous experience in teaching, supervising or mentoring students or colleagues would be beneficial. Ability to provide constructive feedback and support students in developing safe and competent clinical practice. Ability to work collaboratively with academic staff and other clinical educators. Professional Practice: Demonstrated commitment to maintaining professional competence and currency through ongoing clinical practice and professional development. Sound understanding of contemporary oral health practice, infection prevention and control, patient safety, professional standards and ethical responsibilities. Equity and Te Aronui Commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT's Te Aronui journey. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a complete list of publications and grant acquisitions if applicable): please submit a) a cover letter which explains why this particular role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) a statement addressing how you feel you meet some, or all, of the criteria above. All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: As soon as possible Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $49 - $52 per hour For academic enquiries: Contact Dr Heuiwon Han, Head of Department Oral Health han@aut.ac.nz For recruitment enquiries: Please send us an enquiry here or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 8 September 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96552 This role is considered a children’s worker role and will be subject to safety checking as part of the Children’s Act 2014. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96552 Location (s) North Campus, South Campus Employment type (s) Casual (hourly paid) Closes on 08 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Clinical Educator Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) Posted on 25 Aug 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
