    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=xhC6e": {
      "title": "Student Advisor",
      "description": "Student Advisor - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Student Advisor Student Advisor Use your professional skillset in a student facing role Work in a passionate and specialist team Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s award-winning Student Services and Administration directorate is dedicated to delivering exceptional student-centred experiences across the entire learner journey, from enrolment through to graduation and beyond. Bringing together high impact services in student administration, wellbeing and support, governance, systems, and operational delivery, the directorate works collaboratively with academic and professional teams to enable student success and institutional effectiveness. It offers professionals the opportunity to make a meaningful difference in a large, diverse university environment - combining purpose led work, continuous improvement, and a strong focus on equity, service excellence and positive outcomes for students and staff. To learn more about Student Support Services at AUT, please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/student-life/support-services The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi A role for a Student Advisor in the Disability Support Service has become available on AUT's City Campus. This role is permanent and full time, based in the Student Hub. The Disability Support Service plays a critical role in supporting disabled learners to achieve equitable access, participation, and success at AUT. Working within Disability Support Services (DSS), the role provides specialist advice, disability-related accommodations and support to students, while partnering with academic and professional staff to create inclusive learning environments that promote student success. This role reports directly to the Disability Service Manager. As a Student Advisor in the Disability Support Service, you will work directly with students to identify support needs, implement appropriate accommodations, and connect students with accessible learning resources and services. You will provide specialist disability advice across the University and contribute to the continuous improvement of accessibility, inclusion, and student support practices. Key Responsibilities Provide individualised disability support and tailored case management to students. Assess needs and develop Academic Accommodation Plans and other supports. Review and critically evaluate effectiveness of supports to students over their academic studies. Through a holistic case management approach, identify student needs and use appropriate referral pathways. Support the implementation of academic accommodations in partnership with academic staff. Provide guidance on accessibility, and assistive technology, and contribute to universal design principles. Maintain accurate student records and contribute to service reporting requirements. Equip students with skills to advance them beyond life at AUT. Develop strong relationships with internal and external stakeholders to support positive student outcomes. Work at events such as AUT LIVE and other activations promoting the support available to students at AUT. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: 3 or more years' experience in a similar role/ field, A current annual practicing certificate in Social Work, Occupational Therapy or similar or be a Registered NZCER Level C test user, A bachelor's degree or higher in a relevant field Experience in tertiary education, community support or customer service A passion for supporting student success An ability to deliver high-quality, professional service with a culture of customer care An understanding of advisory support delivered via a case management model Extensive experience with technology and relationship management software A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: Immediate start Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $84,538 - $89,677 (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 15th September 2026, at 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96481 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96481 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 15 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Student Services Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 553 - Student Advisor.pdf Posted on 01 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
