    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=IuR3e": {
      "title": "Operations Support & Projects Coordinator",
      "description": "Operations Support & Projects Coordinator - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Operations Support & Projects Coordinator Operations Support & Projects Coordinator Be part of a collaborative faculty team that drives operational excellence Coordinate projects, events and strategic initiatives that make a real impact Provide trusted executive, project and operational support to faculty leadership Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's South Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences is a vibrant, interdisciplinary academic community committed to improving health, wellbeing and environmental sustainability locally and globally. The Faculty brings together leading educators, researchers and practitioners across health sciences, public health, rehabilitation, sport and exercise science, food science, chemistry, biology, biomedical science, and environmental science, with a strong emphasis on applied learning and real-world impact. Staff benefit from close links with industry, iwi, communities and government, opportunities for collaborative and translational research, and a culture that values innovation, equity and social responsibility. The Faculty offers an engaging, supportive environment for talented academics who want their teaching and research to make a meaningful difference in Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are seeking a highly organised and proactive Operations Support & Projects Coordinator to join our Operations Support team within the Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences. Reporting to the Manager – Operations Support, this role provides a blend of project coordination, executive support and operational administration for the Faculty Leadership Team. You will support the planning and implementation of strategic initiatives, coordinate faculty and school events and projects, and ensure the smooth delivery of a wide range of operational activities. This is a varied and fast-paced role where no two days are the same. You'll work closely with senior leaders, professional and academic staff, central AUT teams and external partners and suppliers to help achieve faculty objectives and deliver meaningful outcomes. Key responsibilities include: Coordinating faculty and school projects, initiatives, conferences and events. Providing high-level executive and administrative support to members of the Faculty Leadership Team. Managing diaries, meetings, travel arrangements and correspondence. Preparing agendas, minutes, reports and briefing materials. Monitoring and coordinating key actions, deadlines and communications. Supporting recruitment, onboarding and people-related administrative processes. Assisting with financial administration, purchase orders, invoices and reconciliations. Gathering information and undertaking research to support strategic decision-making. Contributing to continuous improvement initiatives that enhance operational effectiveness. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. You are an experienced administrator and project coordinator who thrives in a collaborative environment and enjoys supporting multiple priorities with professionalism, discretion and efficiency. To be successful in this role, you will have: Relevant tertiary qualifications in business, administration, information technology or a related discipline, or equivalent experience. Proven experience in a coordination, executive support, personal assistant, executive assistant or operational support role. Strong project coordination and event management experience. Advanced Microsoft Outlook skills and proficiency across Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Teams and SharePoint. Experience managing competing priorities and working effectively under pressure. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to build effective relationships at all levels. Strong organisational skills, attention to detail and a commitment to providing high-quality service. Experience working within a large and complex organisation. The ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise sound judgement and demonstrate initiative. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: ASAP Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $76,000 - $84,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 21 September 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96225 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96225 Location (s) South Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 21 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Other Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 920 - Operations Support & Projects Coordinator.pdf Posted on 07 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=MqH2e": {
      "title": "Technical Specialist",
      "description": "Technical Specialist – Clinical Simulation - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Technical Specialist – Clinical Simulation Technical Specialist – Clinical Simulation Be part of establishing AUT’s new state-of-the-art Clinical Simulation Suite supporting the education of New Zealand’s future health workforce. Lead the implementation, commissioning and optimisation of advanced clinical simulation technologies in a newly developed facility. Permanent, full-time role based primarily at AUT’s North Campus (Akoranga). Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is bold and unapologetically different, centred on students and grounded in Knowledge that Works driven by talented, progressive people. We are New Zealand’s newest university, ranked 5-stars by QS Universities 2025 and a place of opportunity where more than 26,000 students with talent and potential succeed, supported by a community of more than 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. Built on collaboration, shared purpose and the values of Pono (fact, truth, reality, integrity), Tika (acting accordingly, doing what is needed, ethical expression), and Aroha (empathy, care, compassion). AUT offers an innovative, forward-thinking environment where committed people work together to improve outcomes for students, communities, and the world. AUT recognises the importance of Te Tiriti, Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership, and contribution across our university and is committed to creating environments where these communities can thrive. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences The Faculty of Health and Environmental Sciences is one of New Zealand’s largest providers of health education, delivering world-class teaching and research across nursing, allied health, sport, science and environmental disciplines. Working closely with industry, government and community partners, the Faculty is committed to preparing graduates who improve the health and wellbeing of Aotearoa New Zealand and beyond. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi This is a permanent, full-time opportunity to play a pivotal role in establishing and operating AUT’s new Clinical Simulation Suite. Reporting to the Senior Manager – Technical Services, you will provide specialist technical expertise supporting simulation-based education across the Faculty, initially focused on Nursing while enabling future multidisciplinary use. Working alongside academic staff, ICT, Estates and external vendors, you will lead the commissioning, operation and continuous improvement of advanced clinical simulation technologies, ensuring the facility is safe, reliable, innovative and ready to support teaching and learning. You will contribute to equipment procurement, installation, systems integration, development of operational procedures, technical training, asset management and quality improvement while providing expert advice on simulation technologies and emerging best practice. This role will directly support AUT’s commitment to technology-enabled learning, student success and Te Aronui by helping create inclusive, culturally responsive learning environments that prepare graduates for contemporary healthcare practice. About you | Ko wai koe If you’re the kind of person who enjoys solving complex technical challenges, embraces innovation, and wants to help shape the future of health education, you’ll thrive in this role. To be successful you will have: Significant experience supporting clinical simulation, healthcare technologies or other complex technical environments. Demonstrated experience commissioning, maintaining and troubleshooting sophisticated technical systems and specialist equipment. Experience working collaboratively with multiple stakeholders to deliver high-quality technical services. Strong problem-solving, organisational and project implementation skills. A relevant tertiary qualification in health technology, biomedical engineering, clinical simulation, science or a related discipline, or equivalent professional experience. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and support for AUT’s Te Aronui framework and Te Tiriti o Waitangi commitments. As a professional member of staff at AUT, you’ll help keep us moving forward. From improving services and implementing new technologies to supporting exceptional student learning experiences, you’ll play an important role in helping AUT deliver world-class health education. You will bring an open, engaging and collaborative approach, demonstrate sound judgement and initiative, and actively contribute to a positive, inclusive and collegial team environment. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll be part of a values-led university that supports you to thrive in your role and career. We offer: Flexible working and a strong, caring culture that supports belonging. Recognition frameworks that reflect your contribution and how you live our values. The tools and trust to make a meaningful difference every day. Māori and Pacific development programmes that strengthen our shared purpose. Cultural capability uplift development programmes for all staff. Professional development and funded study pathways. Free gym membership. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter explaining: why this opportunity and AUT interests you; and how your skills and experience align with the key requirements of the role. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $93,000 - $114,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) - For further information: please send us an enquiry here or call 09 921 9499. Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 17 September 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96124 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96124 Location (s) North Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 17 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Technician Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11000 - Technical Specialist - Clinical Simulation (1).pdf Posted on 03 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=XSL0e": {
      "title": "Te Manu Taki",
      "description": "Te Manu Taki – Māori School Engagement & Partnerships Lead - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Te Manu Taki – Māori School Engagement & Partnerships Lead Te Manu Taki – Māori School Engagement & Partnerships Lead Tēnei te karanga atu nei ki te hunga e mōhiotia ana i roto i o tātou Kura Māori o Tāmaki Makaurau tae atu ki ngā kaupapa Māori e whai pānga ana ki ngā Kura Aunoa o Tāmaki Makaurauo otirā o tātou hāpori Māori kia tonoa mai ki te tūranga nei.  He tūranga tūhonohono tēnei i waenga i Te Wānanga Aronui o Tāmaki Makaurau me ngā Kura Māori, Hāpori Māori anō hoki i a Tāmaki Makaurau.   Me matatau ngā kaitono ki Te Reo Māori, ki ngā Tikanga Māori otirā ngā Kura Māori me o rātou mātāpono, kaupapa, āhuatanga motuhake anō hoki.  Kāti ko te tino whāinga ia, kia whai wāhi ai ngā tauira Māori nō roto mai i ngā Kura Māori ki Te Wānanga Aronui nei, Kura Kaupapa mai, Kura ā Iwi mai, Kura Reo Rua mai, Kura Hāpai Kaupapa mai. Lead AUT’s strategic engagement with Kura Māori and Māori communities. Drive co-designed, culturally affirming partnerships that support Māori student success. Champion Te Aronui – AUT’s Te Tiriti Framework – across outreach and engagement initiatives. Work in a collaborative, values-led environment committed to equity and inclusion Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Brand and Marketing Services looks after how AUT shows up in the world – and why it matters. We’re the stewards of the brand and the engine behind campaigns that build reputation, spark interest and turn curiosity into connection. Working side by side with faculties and professional services, we combine insight, creativity and digital thinking to create joined‑up experiences that feel consistent and human. From first enquiry to enrolment, graduation and long after, we help people see themselves at AUT – and stay connected for the long run. AUT’s Office of Māori Advancement plays a pivotal role in shaping our future by championing Mātauranga Māori and Te Tiriti o Waitangi across the university. Working in close partnership with Māori staff, students, mana whenua, iwi, and Māori communities, the office provides strategic leadership to academic and professional divisions, supports research that delivers real benefits for Māori, and works with faculties to embed Māori pathways and perspectives. It also oversees the vibrant day-to-day operations of AUT’s Ngā Wai o Horotiu marae. Join a team that is deeply values led, community connected, and committed to advancing access, success, and progression for Māori staff and students. To learn more about our Māori at AUT and AUT’s commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi, please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/maori The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are seeking a passionate and experienced leader to join AUT as Te Manu Taki – Kura Māori (Māori Schools) Engagement and Partnership Lead. This pivotal role sits within Brand & Marketing Services and the Office of Māori Advancement, and reports to the Director Future Student with a dotted line into Tu Pouhono.  Applicants will have a high level of familiarity with Kura Māori across Tāmaki Makaurau and beyond and will bring prior experience in engagement with Kura Māori and Hāpori Māori.  Importantly, this role requires Te Manu Taki to have existing relationships that will assist in strengthening connections between Kura Māori and AUT. You will lead exploratory and research-based engagement with Kura Māori, ensuring Māori voices shape AUT’s approach to school partnerships. Acting as a bridge between AUT and Māori education leaders, you will foster relationships grounded in reciprocity and mana-enhancement, co-design culturally responsive pathways, and develop insights that inform AUT’s long-term strategy for Māori student success. This is an exciting role offering the chance to make a meaningful impact on Māori education and AUT’s commitment to Te Tiriti o Waitangi. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: 7–8 years’ experience in Māori engagement, education, or partnership development. Proficiency in Te Reo Māori and deep understanding of tikanga Māori and kawa. Experience applying Māori models of facilitation and engagement (hui, wānanga, kaupapa-based co-design). Strong relationship-building skills with kura, whānau, hapū, iwi, and Māori education networks. Strategic thinking, research capability, and project management skills. A commitment to equity, diversity, and AUT’s Te Aronui journey. An undergraduate degree; additional qualifications in education, Māori development, or related fields are desirable. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: TBD Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $110,000 - $122,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 23 September at 10.30pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 95923 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 95923 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 23 Sep 2026 22:30 Expertise Strategy, Students and Marketing Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 10760 - Manu Taki - Māori  Lead Māori School Engagement and Partnership.pdf Posted on 03 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=SAg8e": {
      "title": "Advanced Robotics Technician",
      "description": "Advanced Robotics Technician - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\r\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\r\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Advanced Robotics Technician Advanced Robotics Technician Work hands-on with AUT’s Unitree G1 EDU humanoid and Go2 quadruped robots Develop and test capabilities including teleoperation, manipulation, LiDAR navigation and simulation Build practical experience across robotics, AI and emerging technologies in a highly varied role Fixed-term, full-time role until 17 December 2027, based at AUT’s [Campus] Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works, AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. The Advanced Robotics Technician will work within AUT’s AI Acceleration Centre, which brings together practical AI, robotics and digital technology initiatives across the University. The team works with researchers, professional staff, students and external partners to explore and apply emerging technologies in ways that support teaching, research, engagement and innovation across AUT. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We are looking for an Advanced Robotics Technician to join AUT in a fixed-term, full-time role until 17 December 2027. This is a highly practical position working directly with AUT’s Unitree G1 EDU humanoid robots and Unitree Go2 quadruped robots. You will help develop, test, operate and demonstrate new robotic capabilities, while taking day-to-day responsibility for ensuring the robots are operational, safe and ready to use. Current development work includes teleoperation, pick-and-place and manipulation tasks, LiDAR-based navigation and simulation using NVIDIA Isaac Lab, with plenty of scope to explore new behaviours, integrations and applications across both humanoid and quadruped platforms. You will spend much of your time working directly with the robots in the lab, but the role also involves preparing, transporting and operating them at AUT events, demonstrations, showcases and other public-facing activities. Key responsibilities include: Operating and maintaining AUT’s Unitree G1 EDU humanoid and Go2 quadruped robots and associated equipment. Preparing, transporting and operating robots at AUT events, demonstrations and showcases. Safely controlling robots during live demonstrations, including teleoperated and pre-programmed behaviours. Developing, integrating and testing new robot behaviours and capabilities using Python and/or C++. Supporting work involving teleoperation, manipulation, pick-and-place, LiDAR navigation and autonomous behaviours. Using simulation environments such as NVIDIA Isaac Lab to develop and test robotic applications. Diagnosing and resolving hardware, software, networking and sensor issues. Working directly with manufacturers on technical troubleshooting, software updates, repairs and replacement parts. Maintaining robot software, configurations, documentation, spare parts and associated equipment. Helping train other staff and students in safe robot operation and demonstration procedures. Ensuring all activities follow AUT’s robotics safety and risk management requirements. You will work with AUT researchers, developers, technical staff and students across robotics, AI and digital technologies. You will also liaise directly with overseas manufacturers when specialist support is required. The role offers significant hands-on experience with advanced robotic platforms and the opportunity to become one of AUT’s key robot operators, with guidance and mentoring from experienced technical staff as you build your skills and take on increasing responsibility. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. AUT staff benefits also include free study options and a personal fund for professional development. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff: https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi, Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. This role would suit someone with a strong practical interest in robotics and emerging technology who enjoys experimenting and troubleshooting, but is also comfortable getting out of the lab and demonstrating technology to others. To be successful in this role, you will ideally have: A Bachelor’s degree in Robotics, Mechatronics, Engineering, Software Engineering, Computer Science, Computer and Information Sciences, or a related discipline. Experience with robotics, automation, embedded systems or autonomous systems through coursework, research, projects, competitions or practical work. Experience programming in Python and/or C++. An understanding of Linux and robotics development environments. An interest in areas such as simulation, sensors, LiDAR, autonomous navigation, teleoperation, computer vision or AI-enabled robotics. Confidence working with people and operating technology in demonstrations, events and public-facing environments. A current New Zealand driver’s licence. A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and support for AUT’s Te Aronui journey. Experience with ROS/ROS2, NVIDIA Isaac Lab/Isaac Sim, Unitree or similar robotic platforms would be an advantage, but is not essential. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role and AUT are of interest to you; and b) addresses how you feel you meet some or all of the key criteria listed above. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: Agreed with the successful candidate Salary Range | Ngā Utu: $62,000 - $81,000 per annum (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information: Please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499. Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 14 October 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96649 Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week. At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96649 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 14 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise IT Experience level (s) Graduate (Qualified, no experience), Experienced (Less than 2 years) More details (document) PD 10635 - Advanced Robotics Technician.pdf Posted on 15 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\r\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\r\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\r\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\r\n            Administrator for further assistance."
