    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=OYH7e": {
      "title": "AUT Online Senior Operations Manager, Auckland CBD",
      "description": "AUT Online Senior Operations Manager, Auckland CBD - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies AUT Online Senior Operations Manager, Auckland CBD AUT Online Senior Operations Manager, Auckland CBD Play a key role in AUT Online’s next phase, supporting the delivery of high-quality online-by-design postgraduate education Bring together operational planning, people, systems and resources across a fast-moving multidisciplinary environment Lead a specialist operations team and embed improvements that support effective, sustainable delivery Fixed-term, full-time role based at AUT's City Campus, with flexible working hours Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT Online is expanding access to university education through flexible, high-quality postgraduate education designed for working professionals. Working in partnership with faculties, we bring together academic expertise, specialist learning design, digital technology and dedicated student recruitment and support to help learners succeed alongside work, whānau and other commitments. Our team supports the end-to-end learner journey from first enquiry through to graduation, with a strong focus on delivering an engaging, connected online learning experience. Working at AUT Online offers the opportunity to collaborate across disciplines, contribute to new ways of working and see the difference your work makes to learners across Aotearoa New Zealand. The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi AUT Online is entering its next phase of growth, and we are seeking an experienced Senior Operations Manager to strengthen the operational planning, financial management, systems and processes that support AUT Online’s delivery. Reporting directly to the Director, AUT Online, you will act as a trusted operational partner and lead our specialist operations team. You will work alongside AUT Online’s Senior Managers and functional leads across programmes, marketing, and student recruitment and retention to translate agreed priorities into coordinated plans and effective delivery. The breadth of this role offers the opportunity to combine operational and people leadership, commercial judgement and practical systems improvement. Central to your success will be your ability to connect work across functions, anticipate dependencies and ensure that resources, processes and systems support shared priorities. Your responsibilities will include: Lead planning and coordination across AUT Online, working with functional leads to clarify responsibilities, align resources, address bottlenecks and manage delivery risks Lead operational budget planning, monitoring, forecasting and reporting, providing analysis and recommendations on financial pressures, resource requirements and opportunities for improvement Lead day-to-day commercial engagement with vendors and contractors Oversee operational systems and processes, identifying opportunities for improvement Lead operational reporting, dashboards and action tracking, providing clear information on performance, risks and matters requiring decisions People leadership, development and resourcing You will build effective relationships with AUT’s Finance, ICT, academic and professional services teams, and support the implementation of approved programmes and initiatives within AUT Online’s operations. You will exercise initiative and judgement within agreed priorities and AUT’s policies and delegations. Through your leadership, planning and people practices, you will give practical effect to Te Aronui, AUT’s Te Tiriti Framework, supporting equitable and mana-enhancing outcomes. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will be an experienced operational leader who combines strong financial and commercial judgement with a practical understanding of people, processes and systems. You build trusted relationships, bring clarity to competing priorities and follow through on agreed actions. You are comfortable leading your own team while working collaboratively across specialist functions. You can influence outcomes through sound advice and effective relationships, and you exercise discretion when handling confidential information. You bring curiosity and openness to new ideas, with the ability to turn improvements into consistent everyday practice. To be successful in this role, you will bring: At least eight years’ overall experience, including a minimum of five years in operational management, business operations or a comparable role within a complex, cross-functional environment At least three years’ experience managing operational budgets, expenditure monitoring, forecasting, procurement, contracts, vendors and commercial administration Experience leading and developing direct reports and coordinating resources, contractors or contributors across multiple functions Demonstrated experience in operational planning, governance reporting and process improvement, including implementing, administering and optimising operational systems and digital tools Strong analytical, organisational and communication skills, with the ability to translate strategic priorities into practical plans and delivery Demonstrated cultural competency, respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi and a commitment to equity and inclusion, with the ability to apply Te Aronui principles in workplace relationships and practice Experience in tertiary education, online learning or another complex service delivery environment is desirable, as is experience supporting organisational growth or transformation. A relevant postgraduate qualification and experience with business intelligence tools, workflow automation or responsible AI adoption would also be an advantage. How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: ASAP Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $117,000-150,000 For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 6 October 2026, 11:55pm Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96587 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96587 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 06 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Administration, Executive, Management & Planning, Finance & Estates, Other Experience level (s) Management More details (document) 11024 - AUT Online Operations Manager.pdf Posted on 15 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=f6v5e": {
      "title": "Lecturers/Senior Lecturers",
      "description": "Lecturers/Senior Lecturers - Built Environment Engineering  (3-year fixed term) - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Lecturers/Senior Lecturers - Built Environment Engineering  (3-year fixed term) Lecturers/Senior Lecturers - Built Environment Engineering  (3-year fixed term) Utilise your academic expertise in the broader area of Built Environment Engineering (incl. Digital Construction and Architectural Technology & Design Management) Contribute to paradigm shift in built environment education, research, and practice Create exceptional student-centred learning experiences while building strong partnerships with industry, professions, iwi and community stakeholders 3-year fixed-term, full-time appointments based at AUT's City Campus in Auckland Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is bold and unapologetically different, centred on students and grounded in Knowledge that Works driven by talented, progressive people. We are New Zealand’s newest university, ranked 5-stars by QS Universities 2025 and a place of opportunity where more than 26,000 students with talent and potential succeed, supported by a community of more than 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. Built on collaboration, shared purpose and the values of Pono (fact, truth, reality, integrity), Tika (acting accordingly, doing what is needed, ethical expression), and Aroha (empathy, care, compassion). AUT offers an innovative, forward-thinking environment where committed people work together to improve outcomes for students, communities, and the world. AUT recognises the importance of Te Tiriti , Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership, and contribution across our university and is committed to creating environments where these communities can thrive. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. The School of Future Environments | Huri te Ao AUT’s newest and fastest-growing school (est. 2020). Bringing together architecture, engineering, construction and emerging technologies, we advance integrated built-environment thinking - shaped by Te Tiriti o Waitangi and Mātauranga Māori, and informed by Te Ao Māori, Moana-nui-a-Kiwa identity and Aotearoa New Zealand’s multicultural diversity. Ranked among the world’s top 260 universities for Architecture and Built Environment in the QS World University Rankings by Subject (2026), we connect research, students and industry to practical outcomes. Our world-renowned scholars develop ecologically-oriented, transdisciplinary programmes across Architecture, Civil, Construction and Architectural Engineering, Construction Management, Creative Technologies and Ecological Urbanism. We work to deliver sustainable, future-ready environments and help address the climate emergency, social justice and complex 21st-century challenges. We have significant interest in AI and the digital transformation of the construction industry, combined with nature-based solutions and (re-)integration of intuitive human cultural factors in complex construction environments. To learn more please visit: https://www.aut.ac.nz/study/study-options/architecture-and-built-environment The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi We have 3-year fixed-term, full-time (37.5 hours per week) opportunities for motivated Lecturers or Senior Lecturers of Built Environment Engineering to make significant impact and develop their career in teaching, research and service. We invite applications from academics and practitioners in Built Environment, Construction, or related disciplines who have the ambition, courage, and expertise to reimagine how we design and build the environments in which we live, work and play! We are particularly interested in expertise in one or more of the following: Digital Design, Engineering and Construction AI in Design and Construction Construction Management for “Construction 5.0” environments Quantity Surveying Structural Engineering Design Management of complex engineering processes Built Environment Engineering pedagogies and practices Integrating Engineering Design with Advanced Technologies . Architectural Intelligence Ecological Sub/Urbanism Design Management and Advanced Professional Practice Research at AUT is central - driving innovation, informing teaching and delivering real-world impact. You will be expected to advance research and practice across the wider school by building an active research profile through publication and dissemination, and by pursuing external funding. You will also engage with government, industry, professional bodies and the community, contributing to school and faculty activities. We embrace practice-led, research-informed teaching for transformative student experiences that uplift communities, using digital resources to enhance learning. These positions support delivery of the School’s built environment engineering and construction programmes across undergraduate and postgraduate study, including Civil, Construction and Architectural Engineering, and Project Management. You will deliver innovative, high-quality teaching and student supervision, and lead and develop courses within the built environment engineering curriculum. Please see the position description available for more information. What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT, you’ll join a values-led university that supports you to thrive . We offer an excellent research environment with contestable research funds , and with guidance available from senior scholars. Benefit from flexible working, a supportive culture, cultural capability development for all staff, and strong growth opportunities – while advancing your impact through clear career pathways, recognition and research and teaching support. To learn more about our competitive staff benefits , please click HERE . About you | Ko wai koe As an academic member of staff at AUT, you’ll blend teaching, research and engagement to create outcomes that have real impact on the world. You’ll work closely with students, collaborate across disciplines and contribute to projects alongside our industry and community partners.  With room to experiment, develop your skills and refine your practice, you’ll be supported to make a practical, impactful contribution to both learning and discovery. You will bring an open, engaging, and collaborative approach, with the flexibility to respond to changing requirements, and actively contribute to a positive and collegial environment. You will demonstrate cultural humility, awareness, and respect when engaging with indigenous peoples and culturally diverse communities. Experience supporting indigenous, equity, or inclusion focused initiatives is highly desirable. The selection criteria sought are: 1. Qualifications: A PhD (or equivalent) in a relevant Built Environment discipline, Architecture or a relevant discipline. 2. AI and the digital transformation of the construction industry Demonstrable interest in AI and the digital transformation of the construction industry, combined with nature-based solutions and a (re-)integration of intuitive human cultural factors in complex construction environments. 3. Teaching: An early career academic will ideally have at least some previous teaching assistant experience. (Lecturer) More experienced candidates will have previous lecturing experience, evidence of curriculum development and preferably experience supervising Master's and/or PhD students. (Senior Lecturer) 4. Research: An early career academic will have the basis of a solid research pipeline. (Lecturer) More experienced candidates will already have a more established research programme and a proven research track record with quality publications and ideally also success in external funding bids. (Senior Lecturer) Evidence of proactively pursuing external research income is desirable. ( Lecturer ) Evidence of securing or contributing to external research income is desirable. ( Senior Lecturer ) 5. Equity and Te Aronui A champion for equity, diversity and inclusion. Supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey ( https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/maori/auts-commitment-to-Te-Tiriti-o-Waitangi ). How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your full academic CV (including a complete list of publications and any grant acquisitions) - please also submit: A cover letter explaining why this role and AUT are of interest, and how your experience aligns with some, or all, of the selection criteria we're seeking above; A research statement (1 page max); And evidence of satisfactory student evaluations and innovation in teaching (2 pages max). All applications must be submitted through the online application process. Further Information: Start Date: Successful candidates would join AUT no later than February 2027 (to be agreed). Term: Successful candidates will secure 3-year fixed-term, full-time academic appointments. Salary Ranges: Lecturers – NZD $94,604 to $112,590; Senior Lecturers – NZD $115,908 to $151,557 (appointment level and salary will be commensurate with skills and experience of the successful candidate). Enquiries: For academic enquiries, contact Professor Ali GhaffarianHoseini, Head of School - ali.ghaffarianhoseini@aut.ac.nz . For recruitment enquiries, contact Mike Wood: AUT Executive Recruitment Partner – mike.wood@aut.ac.nz . Closing date for applications: Monday 12 October at 11.55pm Reference: 96394 At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96394 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Fixed term Closes on 12 Oct 2026 23:55 Expertise Lecturer, Senior Lecturer Experience level (s) Experienced (2 years +) More details (document) PD 11005 - Lecturer - Senior Lecturer - BEE.pdf Posted on 15 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
    },
    "https://careers.aut.ac.nz/jobdetails?ajid=OH18e": {
      "title": "Student Inclusion Manager",
      "description": "Student Inclusion Manager - Rainbow - AUT Students Staff Alumni AUT Ako Study Tawāhi International Oranga Tauira Student\n                                            Life Rangahau Research Whanaukataka Partnerships Mō Mātou About Ako Study Tāwāhi International Oranga Tauira Student Life Rangahau Research Ngātahi Partnerships Mō\n                                Mātou About Sign in Sign in Home About Careers at AUT Job vacancies Student Inclusion Manager - Rainbow Student Inclusion Manager - Rainbow Lead a professional and dynamic service Support the Rainbow student community Permanent, full-time role based at AUT's City Campus Auckland University of Technology (AUT) is New Zealand's newest university and one of its most distinctive. Centred on students and grounded in knowledge that works , AUT is 5-star rated by QS, with more than 27,000 students and 4,000 staff based primarily across three Auckland campuses. It's a place of real opportunity, where the values of Pono, Tika and Aroha shape how talented, progressive people work together – and you'll feel that in the culture, in the collaboration and in the difference the work makes for students, communities and the world. Our community is stronger because of the role Te Tiriti plays in how we operate, and because Māori and Pacific knowledge, leadership and contribution are central to who we are. We embrace diversity in all its forms and are proud to welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. AUT’s award-winning Student Services and Administration directorate is dedicated to delivering exceptional student-centred experiences across the entire learner journey, from enrolment through to graduation and beyond. Bringing together high-impact services in student administration, wellbeing and support, governance, systems, and operational delivery, the directorate works collaboratively with academic and professional teams to enable student success and institutional effectiveness. It offers professionals the opportunity to make a meaningful difference in a large, diverse university environment - combining purpose-led work, continuous improvement, and a strong focus on equity, service excellence and positive outcomes for students and staff. To learn more about Student Support Services at AUT, please click here: https://www.aut.ac.nz/student-life/support-services The Opportunity | Te Whiwhinga mahi An exciting opportunity has become available for a talented professional who enjoys a challenging, fast-paced and progressive environment.  With every day different, you will be prepared to hit the ground running while navigating the demands of this dynamic role.  By providing leadership across Student Services and Administration, the wider University and with external stakeholders to ensure our rainbow student community is supported and enabled to achieve success. You will enjoy building strong internal and external relationships with a variety of stakeholders, representing and maintaining the reputation of the organisation while reflecting a commitment to excellence and vision.  You will be proactive, energetic, and pragmatic; able to demonstrate professional practice while sharing expertise in an educational and engaging way. If you are ready for a challenge, thrive on responsibility, accountability and ownership for your role and actions, along with a professional approach, are flexible, adaptable, assertive, and proactive with high levels of initiative, then we want to hear from you! What we offer | Ngā āhuatanga kei a mātou At AUT you’ll be part of a values-led university with a strong, caring culture, flexible working, generous annual leave and support to thrive in your role and career. We provide the tools, trust, recognition frameworks and cultural capability development programmes to help you make a meaningful contribution. Learn more about our competitive benefits tailored to all staff https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits . https://www.aut.ac.nz/about/careers-at-aut/working-at-aut/staff-benefits About you | Ko wai koe As a professional staff member at AUT, you’ll help our university thrive by improving services, supporting students and staff and driving practical improvements across our campuses. We’re looking for people with energy, curiosity and openness to new ideas who bring a collaborative, adaptable approach and contribute to a positive workplace culture. You’ll also bring cultural humility and respect for Te Tiriti o Waitangi , Indigenous peoples and diverse communities. Experience supporting Indigenous, equity or inclusion-focused initiatives is highly valued. To be successful in this role, you will have: Knowledge and understanding of the contemporary issues and challenges facing students Commitment to the wider rainbow community Experience in case management delivery and providing wellbeing support Ability in developing tactics to support cohorts of students within an integrated pastoral care support framework, with an emphasis on rainbow students and those from diverse backgrounds Innovative solutions and a focus on continuous improvement Experience in monitoring, analysis and providing reporting for senior leadership Proven leadership in the delivery of a high-quality, professional service with a culture of customer care A commitment to equity, diversity and inclusion and supportive of AUT’s Te Aronui journey . How to apply | Me pēhea te tuku tono Along with your CV, please submit a cover letter which a) explains why this role (and AUT) is of interest, and b) addresses how you feel you meet some, or all, of the key criteria listed above. Please note - all applications must be submitted through the online application process on AUT’s careers website. Further Information | Pārongo Anō Start Date: Immediate start Salary Ranges | Ngā Utu: $93,941 - $114,284 (dependent on experience and qualifications) For further information : please send us an enquiry or call 09 921 9499 Closing Date | Te rā aukati: 29th September 2026, at 11:55 pm. Job Reference | Tohutoro Mahi: 96617 *Full-time denotes 37.5 hours per week This role is considered a children’s worker role and will be subject to safety checks as part of the Children’s Act 2014 . At AUT we strive to be a place where people love to work and learn. We are committed to te Tiriti, excellence and inclusivity and aspire to be the University of choice for Māori and Pacific communities. We welcome people of all ethnicities, genders, sexual orientations, religious and political beliefs, socio-economic situations and accessibility needs. Please note that all applications must be submitted through the online application process. For further information, please send us an enquiry here or call 921 9499 . Please note we are happy to answer your questions but we do not accept applications by email. You will need to apply through the standard registration process. Nā tō rourou, nā taku rourou ka ora ai te iwi. With your food basket and my food basket, the people will thrive. Job Details Reference # 96617 Location (s) City Campus Employment type (s) Full-time permanent Closes on 29 Sep 2026 23:55 Expertise Accommodation, General & Administration, Administration, Campus Services, Exam Invigilator, Executive, Management & Planning, Finance & Estates, Health & Safety, Health Centre, Human Resources, IT, International, Library, Other, Public Relations, Registry Services, Security, Maintenance & Facilities Management, Student Services, Technician, Strategy, Students and Marketing Experience level (s) Management More details (document) PD 2533 - Student Inclusion Manager (Rainbow).pdf Posted on 15 Sep 2026 Apply Email this job to a friend Print CONTACT US 0800 AUT UNI (0800 288 864) Outside NZ: +64 9 921 9999 Contact us\n                                online AUT CITY CAMPUS 55 Wellesley Street East, Auckland Central Campus map [PDF, 309.7 KB] AUT NORTH CAMPUS 90 Akoranga Drive, Northcote, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 166.7 KB] AUT SOUTH CAMPUS 640 Great South Road, Manukau, Auckland Campus map [PDF, 207.5 KB] Arion My AUT Canvas Library Careers Copyright Privacy Site map Student\n                                    feedback: complaints, suggestions and compliments Facebook LinkedIn TikTok Douyin Youtube Instagram WeChat Weibo XiaoHongShu This site is powered by Snaphire (www.snaphire.com) This site uses Javascript and is required to search and apply for jobs. Your browser either\n            doesn't support Javascript or it is disabled. If you are on a Corporate Network please contact your\n            Administrator for further assistance."
